      "message": "A device reporting a newer minor version than the stored one, for example openconfig-interfaces 2.6.0 with only 2.5.0 bundled, used to mount on 2.5.0 with a warning and now fails to connect. The user guide covers it, but existing deployments find out only after upgrading. Should the old fallback stay available behind a setting, or be called out in the release notes? Please consider.",
